# /agreement system (deployed 2026-04-28) — single Worker dispatch point.
#
# /contract and /payment 301-redirect to /agreement at the Pages layer.
# The Worker's handleAgreementPage is the single source of truth for the
# kill-switch flow: it reads the agreement_killswitch KV key and branches
# on contract state, including serving legacy contract-legacy.html content
# when the switch is ON for pristine tokens (URL stays on /agreement, only
# the response body changes — no /contract URL is ever Worker-rendered).
#
# DO NOT add a Worker route for /contract or /payment back to wrangler.toml.
# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback intercepts query-string requests to those
# paths before any Worker route can fire when matching static assets exist;
# /contract and /payment redirect to /agreement at the Pages layer to dodge
# that. /agreement and /agreement/* themselves are kept off the Pages SPA
# via _routes.json (added 2026-04-28 after a routing-collision incident
# where a stale agreement/signed.html intercepted real /agreement/signed
# requests, bypassing the Worker's window.__AGREEMENT_DATA__ injection).
# Worker ownership of /agreement and /agreement/* is now enforced by
# _routes.json, not by accident. The agreement.html shell at the repo
# root is still Pages-served and is fetched by the Worker as a subrequest
# (see src/agreement.ts handleAgreementPage / handleAgreementSignedPage).
/contract                  /agreement  301
/contract/*                /agreement  301
/payment                   /agreement  301
/payment/*                 /agreement  301
